{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"octahedral-auburn-sunfish","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"# Deploy manifests do not cover the host disk-cap scripts\n\n## What\n\n`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`'s `*_PATHS` manifests do not list either of the ADR 0112 host\ncap scripts:\n\n- `infra/scripts/docker-storage-cap.sh` (story `9183-aaae-667d-45e6`)\n- `infra/scripts/journald-cap.sh` (story `e956-b1c3-45b9-4016`)\n\nBoth are consumed by `infra/scripts/observability.sh` (`--print-env`, and for journald\n`--check-active`) and installed by `infra/scripts/compose-up.sh` (`--install`). Those two\nCONSUMERS are covered — `observability.sh` by `OBS_PATHS`, `compose-up.sh` by\n`MATERIALIZER_PATHS` — but the cap scripts themselves are in neither.\n\n## Consequence\n\nA commit that changes ONLY a cap value (the exact edit ADR 0112 decision 6 says an operator\nshould be able to make) changes no path in any manifest, so autodeploy signals nothing and the\nnew ceiling is not applied until some unrelated change happens to trigger the same action. The\nfiles themselves do reach the box with the checkout, so this is a missed TRIGGER rather than a\nmissing file — but it is the drift class `scripts/check_deploy_manifest.py` exists for.\n\n`check_deploy_manifest.py` does not catch it: it derives its expected path set from\nDockerfile/compose references and from filename conventions (`materialize-*.sh`,\n`*-entrypoint.sh`, `compose-up.sh`), and `*-cap.sh` matches none of them.\n\n## Why this is not fixed inside either story\n\nEditing `autodeploy.sh` was outside both stories' declared `file_impact`, and adding a path\nthere invalidates a signed plan-review attestation whose currency basis IS the file impact.\nThe gap is shared by both scripts, so it is one change here rather than half a change in each.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Both cap scripts are listed in the manifests whose actions actually consume them, or an\n      in-tree comment records why a given manifest deliberately excludes them.\n- [ ] `scripts/check_deploy_manifest.py` derives `infra/**/*-cap.sh` (or an equivalent rule)\n      so a future host-cap script cannot be added without manifest coverage.\n- [ ] A test proves the new derivation is non-vacuous: removing a cap script from the manifests\n      fails the gate.","id":"5246-2ec0-1fa6-4637","parent_id":"","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["infra","disk-ceiling","autodeploy"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Deploy manifests do not cover the host disk-cap scripts"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788563252907784641,"uuid":"8bbe02b9-7130-4255-a5d8-4e12cbbd5f94"}